       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg four times daily comes to 9,600 mg per day. The usual maximum for an adult is 3,200 mg per day under physician supervision, and 1,200 mg per day for over-the-counter use. This order is three times the maximum. It risks GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant 2400 mg as the total daily dose. Here are some common regimens:\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), which is common for mild to moderate pain\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm the dose if 2400 mg per administration is intended. It's worth reviewing the order with your supervising resident or attending before I enter it. I can add a note to the order, such as \"take with food.\""
